From 73ca170aaca64dda9c4b602364a94fc3d0b24cd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ed Schofield <ed@aicharmers.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:12:13 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: Keep both iMac 5K tiles at one colour depth

The iMac 5K panel is driven as two tiles: the left by eDP on link 0, the
right by DP on link 1. With the left tile's stream at 8 bpc and the
right's at 10 bpc, the right half of the panel loses its image, although
both streams stay enabled, scan out and keep their links trained. At
8/8 and at 10/10 bpc both halves show.

Each tile's connector has its own "max bpc" property. A change on one
tile gives that tile's stream a new depth and leaves the other stream
unchanged, so a single property change reaches the unequal state.

Do not attach "max bpc" to either tile, so that neither can be changed
alone. Both then take the depth from their EDIDs, as they do by default.
Other connectors are unchanged.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
index 6e1b81078..a8660b221 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
@@ -3310,7 +3310,8 @@ void amdgpu_dm_connector_init_helper(struct amdgpu_display_manager *dm,
 				adev->mode_info.underscan_vborder_property,
 				0);
 
-	if (!aconnector->mst_root)
+	/* iMac 5K: unequal tile depths lose the right tile's image; no per-tile cap. */
+	if (!aconnector->mst_root && !(dm->imac5K_support && link_index <= 1))
 		drm_connector_attach_max_bpc_property(&aconnector->base, 8, 16);
 
 	aconnector->base.state->max_bpc = 16;
